@@ -0,0 +1,49 @@
+Feature: DOM identity preservation
+  As a browser acceptance suite
+  I want DOM nodes to stay attached across state changes
+  So that element references taken before an interaction remain valid
+
+  @contract
+  Scenario: Toggle checkbox preserves the li element identity
+    Given I have a todo "Buy milk"
+    When I capture the li element for "Buy milk"
+    And I click the toggle checkbox for "Buy milk"
+    Then the captured li element is still attached to the DOM
+
+  @contract
+  Scenario: Unmarking a completed todo preserves the li element identity
+    Given I have a completed todo "Buy milk"
+    When I capture the li element for "Buy milk"
+    And I click the toggle checkbox for "Buy milk"
+    Then the captured li element is still attached to the DOM
+
+  @contract
+  Scenario: Toggle-all preserves all li element identities
+    Given I have todos "Buy milk" and "Walk dog"
+    When I capture all li elements
+    And I click the toggle-all checkbox
+    Then every captured li element is still attached to the DOM
+
+  @contract
+  Scenario: Toggle-all clearing completed state preserves all li element identities
+    Given I have todos "Buy milk" and "Walk dog"
+    And all todos are marked completed
+    When I capture all li elements
+    And I click the toggle-all checkbox
+    Then every captured li element is still attached to the DOM
+
+  @contract
+  Scenario: Marking a todo while filtered does not detach its li element
+    Given I have a todo "Buy milk"
+    And the "Active" filter is selected
+    When I capture the li element for "Buy milk"
+    And I click the toggle checkbox for "Buy milk"
+    Then the captured li element is still attached to the DOM
+
+  @contract
+  Scenario: Clear completed preserves remaining li element identities
+    Given I have todos "Buy milk" and "Walk dog"
+    And "Walk dog" is completed
+    When I capture the li element for "Buy milk"
+    And I click "Clear completed"
+    Then the captured li element for "Buy milk" is still attached to the DOM
\ No newline at end of file
